// Map: a literal's value is in its range, with no lookup of the literal
// written. Silicon does not prove this (its range axiom triggers on a lookup
// `m[k]`); Helium does, with Z3, from the terms its e-graph instances add.
method literal_value_in_range() {
  assert 10 in range(Map(1 := 10, 2 := 20))
}
